	(text "Analog to digital converter stage. The ADC measures voltages between\n-2.5 --- 2.5 V. The ADC has its own 2.5 V voltage reference\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 486.41 179.07 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0b3af911-7b68-4fd4-93b3-b877ec60c3e2")
	)
	(text "Pair of optacouplers are used to manually switch on the \nlinear regulators from the Pico GPIO pins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 49.022 453.898 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "443951ad-715c-471b-854b-c5adceb1bcfa")
	)
	(text "The microcontroller, Raspberry Pi Pico controls the whole operation\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 463.804 471.932 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "47cebdbc-1a88-4164-90d2-b3881a5ab5b0")
	)
	(text "Pair of linear regulators produce 12 V and 2.5 V voltage rails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 125.73 360.172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "637e72cb-75a4-4b97-bd75-37077cfbaad3")
	)
	(text "Filtering stage for the temperature diode measurement. The voltage is converted to a single ended signal,\nsplit in half and filtered through a low-pass filter into an ADC. The instrumentation amp has very high R_G,\nwhich yields unity gain. The resistor could even be removed for full unity gain\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 441.452 303.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "65f259c6-ac83-4af6-a490-c8025ffaa122")
	)
	(text "Pair of analog switches. The first switch determines which direction\nthe current flows and the second one determines between \nwhich nodes the current flows"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 150.114 35.306 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6fd5b801-3761-45df-bcc0-570c95b099b3")
	)
	(text "Current source to the Hall element. IN- pin is connected to a 4:1 multiplexer,\nwhich allows us to choose the source current manually\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 138.43 184.404 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "70a1a88a-e5f7-4245-9f85-3c7e9fc1a7fa")
	)
	(text "3 10x molex picoblade connectors. \nEach connector has a PRESCENSE-pin,\nwhich connects to a GPIO-pin pulled high. \nWhen connected, the pin\nconnects to ground and pulls the GPIO-pin low,\nindicating that the connector is plugged in"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 381.254 186.436 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "799f168a-b9ca-4b0e-8928-02464959a45c")
	)
	(text "0 Ohm resistor connected to Pico ADC.\nThis allows to internally test the voltage \nof this pin to see if the current saturates.\nCan also not be populated if function is not \ndesired"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.876 202.438 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "79c6fd1c-71bb-4beb-acd7-1e1b0e9c2c24")
	)
	(text "Set of 8 4:1 multiplexers. Each analog measurement signal is \nconnected to one of the multiplexers and a 2 bit control signal controls\nwhich connector the signals connect to\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.29 242.824 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "adb6abd1-05be-4025-95b7-01a46e5e82d2")
	)
	(text "Current source to the temperature measurement diode. \nWill produce a steady current of 10 µA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 37.592 311.912 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c804c4f6-f9be-4d34-aa86-6a4f403641c9")
	)
	(text "Filter stage of the Hall voltage. A set of switches determine which nodes to measure voltage \nbetween. The signal is then filtered, amplified and converted to a single ended signal through \na second order band-pass filter. The gain is simulated to 40 dB and the resonance frequency is \nsimulated to around 7000 Hz"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 605.028 29.718 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c8344285-23f0-4447-93ec-217ea05cd802")
	)
	(text "Optocoupler controlling the enable pin of the 2.5 V regulator\nto manually switch on the voltage. This acts as a reference for \nthe current supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.042 360.426 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d487d07f-7fe1-4af3-bec4-bddb8d4c7d39")
	)
	(text "Pair of linear regulators produce -12 V and -2.5 V voltage rails"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127.508 458.724 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d523976d-568b-4b18-aff3-3d48f9b4b981")
	)
	(text "Resistance values corresponds to currents of 3000 - 300 - 30 µA\nfor R14-16. R17 yields 8.3 mA, which is close to the maximum current\nwe reasonably can push into the Hall sensor.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 178.308 196.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f82dc8d1-93b9-4bf1-8647-e733bd259fd6")
	)
	(text "15 V DC Power supply into +/-15V \n \n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 83.312 467.614 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "fffcc311-a0ef-4804-98ec-f45a546e7033")
	)
